{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Kwg3UM4ypNotMExSX8xjvg","type":"tool_result","content":"Declared features        : <none>\nCombinations to verify   : 1\nFeature combination: <no features>\nOK: every C symbol is exported by the Rust .so (10 symbols)\ntest result: ok. 12 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.01s\ntest result: ok. 3 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\ntest result: ok. 17 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.07s\nOK: tests passed for [<no features>]\nALL FEATURE COMBINATIONS VERIFIED\nexit=0","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9db91dee-5ac9-4167-972b-789e6464bd1a","uuid":"b439249c-3028-4222-b63b-3df423b1d7a1","timestamp":"2026-08-19T10:58:51.604Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Declared features        : <none>\nCombinations to verify   : 1\nFeature combination: <no features>\nOK: every C symbol is exported by the Rust .so (10 symbols)\ntest result: ok. 12 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.01s\ntest result: ok. 3 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\ntest result: ok. 17 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.07s\nOK: tests passed for [<no features>]\nALL FEATURE COMBINATIONS VERIFIED\nexit=0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vrdy5x4qzygsukge3uz3vnxwvtljqwknr5xy2zac5jrzxh3s4caq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass, and I found and fixed one real translation bug.\n\n## The bug: `c2Dot` returned the wrong NaN payload\n\n`c2Dot` is `return a.x * b.x + a.y * b.y;`. On x86-64, SSE `mulss`/`addss` propagate the **destination** operand when it's a NaN, falling back to the source only otherwise. The reference C build (`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so GCC runs at `-O0`) emits *swapped* destinations:\n\n```\nmulss %xmm0,%xmm1   ; a.x * b.x        dest = a.x\nmulss %xmm2,%xmm0   ; b.y * a.y        dest = b.y     <-- swapped\naddss %xmm1,%xmm0   ; y_prod + x_prod  dest = y_prod  <-- swapped\n```\n\nThe Rust wrote the expression in source order, so LLVM picked `a.y` and `x_prod` as destinations:\n\n| input | C (`-O0`) | Rust (before) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `a=(0.0, 0x7FC00000)`, `b=(0.0, 0xFFC00000)` | `0xFFC00000` | `0x7FC00000` |\n\n`c2Dot` is a public export returning `float`, so this is directly observable. Fixed with explicit `mulss`/`addss` helpers that encode x86 NaN priority and quieting in the *source* — so it's now identical in debug **and** release, rather than depending on instruction selection. I confirmed the analogous `-O0` quirk in `c2CircletoCircle`'s `A.r + B.r` is *not* observable (the value only feeds a comparison), and that `c2Sub`/`c2Maxv`/`c2Minv` already matched.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n**`cargo test` does not relink the `cdylib`.** My first fix appeared to change nothing because the tests kept loading a stale `libcollided_lib.so`. I added an mtime staleness guard to the harness that aborts with a rebuild hint — without it this trap silently invalidates the whole suite.\n\n**Both `.so`s export identical symbol names,** and C's `c2Maxv` calls `c2V` through its PLT. I verified via mutation that there's no `dlopen` interposition (breaking Rust's `c2V` leaves C's results correct), and locked it in with a test asserting all 10 symbols resolve to distinct addresses per library — otherwise the differential assertions would be vacuous.\n\n## Results\n\n- **Symbol parity:** 10/10 C symbols exported by Rust, diff empty, no stubs, in both debug and release. Undefined symbols are only libc/unwinder imports from `libstd`.\n- **Configurations:** `Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, and `c_src` has no `#ifdef` or CMake `option()` — exactly **one** valid combination. `run_verification.sh` derives the feature set mechanically and would loop the full power set if any existed.\n- **Phase B:** 17/17 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass. **Phase C:** 13/13 `ERRORS.md` rows pass (asserting the exact `0` sentinel from both, plus that C really returns `0`, so agreement-on-wrong can't pass).\n- **32 tests**, ~2.1M bit-exact comparisons (`to_bits()`, never float `==`).\n- **Mutation-tested: 13 injected bugs, 13 detected, 0 missed.**\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `tests/`, `run_verification.sh`, `mutation_check.sh`. `c_src/` sources are unmodified (only `build/` added, as the given build command requires).\n\nOne caveat on the fix: it pins the NaN payload to GCC's `-O0` codegen, which is what the documented build command produces. At `-O2` GCC picks the natural operand order instead, so if the reference `.so` were ever built optimized, `c2Dot`'s NaN payloads would diverge again. Everything else is optimization-independent."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":452,"cache_read_input_tokens":123960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":452,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9db91dee-5ac9-4167-972b-789e6464bd1a","uuid":"62943b61-82c1-4a52-b426-d3bfe333f669","timestamp"